ercentage of the duration for starting a bend; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last-beat the percentage for ending it. The default choices are:","type":"text"}],"title":"sound","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend type is used in guitar notation and tablature. A single note with a bend and release will contain two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bend elements: the first to represent the bend and the second to represent the release. The shape attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguishes between the angled bend symbols commonly used in standard notation and the curved bend symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commonly used in both tablature and standard notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBend"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLBend","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBend"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend/Shape-swift.enum":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Shape"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bend-shape type distinguishes between the angled bend symbols commonly used in standard notation and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"curved bend symbols commonly used in both tablature and standard notation."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLBend.Shape","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbend\/shape-swift.enum","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBend\/Shape-swift.enum","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Shape"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBend/init(alter:content:withBar:shape:position:font:co